<title>USA: Granite Construction to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Granite Construction to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>WATSONVILLE, Calif. 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Granite Construction Inc said its board of directors authorized the buyback of about 100,000 shares, to be purchased on the open market at management's discretion.</p>
<p>It said the repurchased shares will be held in the corporate treasury and used to cover future obligations under its future or current Employee Stock Ownership Plan, or for other corporate purposes.</p>
<p>As of March 3, the company had 18,133,153 common shares outstanding, and its employees held almost 32 percent of that amount.</p>
